<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maxtla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1428">1428</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maxtla was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tepanecs">Tepanec</a> ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azcapotzalco">Azcapotzalco</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-mexico">Valley of Mexico</a> in the fifteenth century. After seizing power following his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tezozomoc">Tezozomoc</a>'s death in 1426, he allegedly had the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> ruler murdered. The Mexica, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texcoco">Texcoco</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlacopan">Tlacopan</a> formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Triple Alliance</a> against him, and his defeat marked the foundation of the Aztec Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maxtla.jpg" alt="Maxtla" width="320" height="313" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Akapochtli · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maxtlatl.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
